{"title":"2023 WSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many ordered triplets of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d80414f2f94f70731e91b6e12c4e6934c8fa65de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5e11d942d5ae627aeaef5cd3d8d69c29b376074.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + 2ab + b^2 = c^2 - 6c + 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/1/7712c792a64408470885361f1ce59724e23e250c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2 \\le a, b, c \\le 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Taking the square root, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/d/46dfcfa2c9a2e6b979d2a8f533613efc116ac0ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|a+b|=|c-3|=d.\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" /> For each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/2/992539597638cf17632585ce1cac13130e8a7657.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\neq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8c4add7796dda048ef6029ed7018b2059fa75b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a+b|=d\\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/8271d4342b38d2ab38bb626ffad8b9dae00b5e2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, there are only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e7d81486409fc9e8f811a5052b2f2a6200c977a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a+b|=d=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />. So, there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cfc850eb300161906e6f2b9854a3632120520f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9\\cdot10+5=\\boxed{95}\\]\" width=\"125\" height=\"23\" /> such ordered triplets.\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018024247\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.008 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 53/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2458/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31908:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018024247 and revision id 273839. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}